      "side": 1,
      "message": "It looks like this is trying to re-implement [`fnmatch`](https://developer.apple.com/library/archive/documentation/System/Conceptual/ManPages_iPhoneOS/man3/fnmatch.3.html).\n\nInstead I think you should use the implementation used by `FileEnumerator::IsPatternMatched(...)` (to support Windows) and use the method in your code and in `FileEnumerator(...)`.\n\nSo two files `pattern_posix.cc`\n\n```\nbool FilePathMatchPattern(const base::FilePath\u0026 path, base::FilePath::StringViewType pattern) {\n  return pattern.empty() ||\n    fnmatch(pattern.c_str(), path.value().c_str(), FNM_NOESCAPE) \u003d\u003d 0;\n}\n```\n\nand `pattern_win.cc`\n\n```\nbool FilePathMatchPattern(const base::FilePath\u0026 path, base::FilePath::StringViewType pattern) {\n  return pattern.empty() ||\n    PathMatchSpec(ToWCharT(\u0026src.value()), ToWCharT(\u0026pattern)) \u003d\u003d TRUE;\n}\n```\n\nthen use `FilePathMatchPattern(...)` in your code and in `FileEnumerator`.",
      "revId": "87e27295a6ceba117329fce44c3ca866d1fad14f",
      "serverId": "c360c8e5-7aa8-3905-a7a0-810934766dac"
    },
